{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1789215427999125507,"compiled_state":{"alias":"sudorific-beautiful-ballpython","assignee":null,"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":1},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1789199516004013001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context\n\n`make worktree` computes `target_dir=\"$(if $(dir),$(dir),../$(name))\"`, so with no\n`dir=` it creates the worktree as a SIBLING of the checkout. For a clone at\n`~/rebar` that writes directly into the home directory, which is the main source\nof the scattered worktrees this workstation has accumulated.\n\nAn agent filesystem sandbox is now active on this workstation (Claude Code,\nCodex, and Copilot CLI). Its write allowlist covers the repo under work plus\n`~/worktrees` and `~/scratch`; the home directory root is NOT writable. The\ndefault path is therefore no longer merely untidy — it is refused by the kernel,\nand `make worktree` fails for every agent session that does not pass `dir=`.\n\n## Situation being documented\n\nThe fix was committed directly to local `main` WITHOUT a rebar ticket trailer and\nWITHOUT landing through Gerrit, deliberately bypassing the commit gate.\n\nJustification: the broken default is a hard stop for any new agent session on\nthis machine — the first `make worktree` fails, and the failure reads as a broken\nMakefile rather than a sandbox denial, which is a slow and misleading diagnosis.\nLanding through the normal path would take longer than the window in which new\nsessions start hitting it. The trade was made knowingly.\n\nConsequence: local `main` now carries a commit with no Change-Id and no ticket\ntrailer, so the repo root CANNOT be pushed until this is reconciled. That is\naccepted as temporary. This ticket is the record of that state.\n\n## Plan\n\nReconcile the out-of-band commit through the normal path: re-author the change on\na proper branch with a Change-Id and this ticket's trailer, land it via Gerrit,\nand reset local `main` to the landed commit so the root is pushable again.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `make worktree name=<branch>` with no `dir=` creates the worktree under\n      `~/worktrees/rebar/<branch>` and provisioning succeeds.\n- [ ] An explicit `dir=<path>` still overrides the default.\n- [ ] The target's help text and usage message state the new default.\n- [ ] The change is landed through Gerrit with a Change-Id and a rebar-ticket\n      trailer referencing this ticket.\n- [ ] Local `main` no longer carries the unreferenced commit, and the repo root\n      can be pushed.\n\n## Verification\n\nRun `make worktree name=tmp-verify`, confirm it lands under\n`~/worktrees/rebar/tmp-verify` with a usable `.venv`, then remove it with\n`git worktree remove` and `git branch -D`. Confirm `git log origin/main..main`\nis empty once reconciled.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":0,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["worktree","sandbox","tooling"],"ticket_id":"9b4a-89fb-3328-497e","ticket_type":"bug","title":"make worktree default path writes into the home directory and is now blocked by the agent sandbox","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["717a076b-4fa6-4bd7-8355-bb5bf846bd6d"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1789215427999125507,"uuid":"ebcf823f-bc45-4672-a11d-7e22bcd882fc"}